import tests/games/geometry_dash/generator.dl

set course to an empty dash level
add (a dash obstacle of kind (the solid tile) at -200.0 (the dash floor) sized 2000.0 by 400.0) to the address of course
set body to a fresh cube
step (the address of body) through course holding jump true
require condition (body's y < the dash floor - the cube size) reporting "Grounded jump failed"
require condition (body's jumps = 1) reporting "Jump count is incorrect"
loop 8 times:
    step (the address of body) through course holding jump true
require condition (body's jumps = 1) reporting "Holding jump caused an air jump"
require condition (body's rotation > 0.0) reporting "The cube did not rotate in the air"
loop while not body's grounded:
    step (the address of body) through course holding jump false
require condition (body's rotation mod 90.0 = 0.0) reporting "Landing did not square the cube"
step (the address of body) through course holding jump true
require condition (body's jumps = 2) reporting "Held input did not jump after landing"

set course's count to 0
add (a dash obstacle of kind (the solid tile) at 300.0 500.0 sized 100.0 by 110.0) to the address of course
set body to a fresh cube
set body's x to (300.0 - the cube size) - 1.0
step (the address of body) through course holding jump false
require condition (body's dead) reporting "Hitting a wall was not lethal"
set body to a fresh cube
set body's x to 320.0
set body's y to (500.0 - the cube size) - 1.0
set body's velocity to 3.0
set body's grounded to false
step (the address of body) through course holding jump false
require condition (body's grounded and not body's dead) reporting "Landing on a block was not allowed"
require condition (body's y = 500.0 - the cube size) reporting "The cube did not land on the block top"
set body to a fresh cube
set body's x to 320.0
set body's y to 611.0
set body's velocity to -6.0
set body's grounded to false
step (the address of body) through course holding jump false
require condition (body's dead) reporting "Hitting a ceiling was not lethal"

set spike to a dash obstacle of kind (the spike tile) at 300.0 578.0 sized 28.0 by 32.0
set body to a fresh cube
set body's x to (300.0 - the cube size) + 2.0
require condition (not (body touches spike spike)) reporting "The forgiving spike edge killed the player"
set body's x to 300.0
require condition (body touches spike spike) reporting "The spike tip did not kill the player"
set course's count to 0
set body to a fresh cube
loop 200 times:
    step (the address of body) through course holding jump false
require condition (body's dead) reporting "Falling into a gap was not lethal"
close the address of course
print line "Dash physics passed"
